    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186059716,
      "id": "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628",
      "title": "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b7635d14-8a69-5926-afe2-8ee962b4290b",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}}{|3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v} &= 3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}9+(-14) \\\\ 6+(6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}| &= \\sqrt{(-5)^2+(12)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{169} \\\\\n&= 13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}}{|3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot (3\\mathbf{t}+2\\mathbf{v}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5}{13} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0e8d0e33-d267-545c-8770-728413aab03b",
