    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c5f79427-68f1-5ce7-b89e-59b84040be3e",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ - 3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}}{|3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b} &= 3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ - 3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ - 3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-15+(12) \\\\ 0+(- 3 \\sqrt{3})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ - 3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}| &= \\sqrt{(-3)^2+(- 3 \\sqrt{3})^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{36} \\\\\n&= 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}}{|3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ - 3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
