    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b05e2418-a103-5214-9882-5bc81e51e01c",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{s}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ \\sqrt{21}\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}}{|2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s} &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ \\sqrt{21}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ \\sqrt{21}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}10+(-8) \\\\ 0+(\\sqrt{21})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{21}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}| &= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(\\sqrt{21})^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}}{|2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (2\\mathbf{r}+\\mathbf{s}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{21}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
